{"step_index":1210,"source":"MODEL","type":"GENERIC","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-22T01:24:01Z","content":"Created At: 2026-09-22T04:24:01+03:00\nCompleted At: 2026-09-22T04:24:05+03:00\nThe search for \"\"unstructured-transform-client\" parse document extract python\" returned the following summary:\nThe `unstructured` library and its associated `unstructured-client` (often used via the `unstructured-client` Python SDK) are designed to parse complex documents (PDFs, DOCX, HTML, images, etc.) and extract structured data[1][2][3].\n\n### Core Concepts\n*   **Partitioning:** The process of breaking a document into \"elements\" (e.g., `Title`, `NarrativeText`, `ListItem`, `Table`, `Image`)[4][2].\n*   **Extraction:** The newer \"Extract\" workflow allows you to pull specific fields as structured data directly from those documents[5][3].\n*   **Modes:** \n    *   **Local:** Uses local processing (no API costs) but may require system-level dependencies for complex file types[1][6].\n    *   **API:** Uses the Unstructured API for advanced AI-based OCR and complex layout analysis[1][7].\n\n---\n\n### Basic Usage Patterns\n\n#### 1. Using the `unstructured` Library (Local)\nFor local partitioning, you primarily use the `partition` function[8].\n\n```python\nfrom unstructured.partition.auto import partition\n\n# Partition a document into elements\nelements = partition(filename=\"example.pdf\")\n\n# Iterate through and print elements\nfor element in elements:\n    print(f\"{element.category}: {element.text}\")\n```\n\n#### 2. Using the `unstructured-client` (API)\nWhen using the SDK to interact with the Unstructured API for more advanced processing or extraction, you typically use the `UnstructuredClient`[3][6].\n\n```python\nimport os\nfrom unstructured_client import UnstructuredClient\nfrom unstructured_client.models import operations, shared\n\n# Initialize client\nclient = UnstructuredClient(api_key_auth=os.getenv(\"UNSTRUCTURED_API_KEY\"))\n\n# Example: Using the SDK to parse a file\nwith open(\"document.pdf\", \"rb\") as f:\n    req = operations.PartitionRequest(\n        partition_parameters=shared.PartitionParameters(\n            files=shared.Files(\n                content=f.read(\n<truncated 908 bytes>\npw2gfl4ioYer0g_a5rkeBBoqLJ8_DeixD_8wB_fgr0eNc0dBoZ3VJhlEYAkeumZ2OZCMNtjvMhte4uT6lWsWdaEVrDtbP3vq4_0T790313Rl1a4sQyc6Fgd)\n[2] [readthedocs.io](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQE4TLRfvlL_lVDSp9wcR6wmv3Zc1KO3uQiq4Kml1g9VMTkR_CDgeKSVEuWKlGitztnSNhiCI2TqjAlZaQjwWBc544vbgRITBmK2zj5dFr_JA74mrAUTJ-5a9QKI-DzEf7uVTQj-h05FJcPGWi4F1nO-S2HlvF4U61ZfjG5wwXJrQhNpKQ==)\n[3] [unstructured.io](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQGC3u-zjmFqtwy5TsLbm50TH6zNEBzqtPFzziQg2s2TP2nr_XVzTaSXwrh1ieJDIOx4tv1OWw6nnkLaJZLe9vpR5O-RAYNrrGUpVmFSahT23lfGZ8RxC3GrYfmcXpcHFzYYN0RVrfQ=)\n[4] [readthedocs.io](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQFey9eVcS_DsqRRaMjtYn0c2NyWmzDDBPfziIjoCssHOHlklrRkrkveidlxy86qqSlxdVAJ6_xWl0avPPDnNUemcduSQPBgBGCq1wDQkTh1kGKa1gcTj5za_CwbQ5nA9XARzUC42w9-_-motW4j1_SrvoBNTCo30_rfF2oR)\n[5] [unstructured.io](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQHLbG_RX25Fl9iVy9iA2K3M8CpK229BBxkO9WFXsSSK5pbf34d5Jpe_W_XGp_H30yD46Cc26fCdEisgmiBrPXFQeUEpj519-NEo8r-Tj2CuepNQvuEOHkzSX_A6qopOpqyWNjjXj8PxJVBe)\n[6] [langchain.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQHnKkRcOJkZXZ1DKXbiWWkfltO8V5QH3lOK2FuvX221SoVKbL5waw9bnT_CHXvPtI6Kc-I4Z-y4yxkPARTs8xZPV4N6ZczBn6y-COJ6PbV-s08dOGfcN5zLbb-sATX-IYolYIhVYZBnbKhVSwacWxg2YUgJqOKjPMHUZMOk1GBkq7JK9b7ZM8p9tgLh)\n[7] [youtube.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQH2ZxqXagQ9Vw6-vE9YH2fEOtOcy74mE0OpsS6nZDf4FoFCfoJEKcYFjoL4kim0JBDzuXNaQlXi9zbhry0H51p0sQKrCOeY_gp_gjgF4iTIuJbBEUCkYZLgZ92wkPnK_Ypb)\n[8] [pypi.org](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQHmAdKcC6n1VI0EkwN7VNsmQY-keUyMTQdldAvCtAF0NDD