{"step_index":1248,"source":"MODEL","type":"GENERIC","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-22T01:26:49Z","content":"Created At: 2026-09-22T04:26:49+03:00\nCompleted At: 2026-09-22T04:26:52+03:00\nThe search for \"\"https://api.unstructured.io\" \"structured_data_extractor\"\" returned the following summary:\nThe `structured_data_extractor` is a core component within the Unstructured.io platform and API designed to transform unstructured documents (such as PDFs, emails, and forms) into clean, structured JSON output[1][2][3].\n\n### Key Concepts\n*   **Purpose:** Unlike standard partitioning, which converts files into generic document elements, the `structured_data_extractor` allows you to define a specific target JSON schema[2]. It then extracts only the precise data fields you require from your source files[4][2].\n*   **Methods:** It supports two primary subtypes for extraction[5][3]:\n    *   **LLM (Large Language Model):** Uses language models to extract data based on a provided JSON schema or plain-language extraction guidance[6][2].\n    *   **Regex:** Uses regular expression patterns to identify and extract specific data, such as prices or ID numbers[7][8][3].\n\n### Usage in the API\nWhen using the Unstructured API, the `structured_data_extractor` is typically configured as a node within a job's processing pipeline[9][5]. \n\n**Example Configuration Snippet:**\nIn API requests, you define the extractor within the `job_nodes` array[9][10]:\n\n```json\n{\n  \"name\": \"Extractor\",\n  \"type\": \"structured_data_extractor\",\n  \"subtype\": \"llm\",\n  \"settings\": {\n    \"schema_to_extract\": {\n      \"json_schema\": { ... },\n      \"extraction_guidance\": \"...\"\n    },\n    \"provider\": \"openai\",\n    \"model\": \"gpt-5-mini\",\n    \"output_mode\": \"extracted_data_only\"\n  }\n}\n```\n\n### How to Access\n*   **API/SDK:** You can integrate the extractor programmatically using the Unstructured Python SDK or by sending requests directly to the Unstructured API[9][3].\n*   **UI:** It is also available via the Unstructured workflow designer and the Start page for local file processing[5][3].\n\nSources:\n[1] [unstructured.io](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AU\n<truncated 488 bytes>\nd.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQHascvcwqSXbp-FAe5Li_sqyS2v6BFKe1wQVCifM2WvcON3oGu76zfmjQGV4voyKXb_FoNwDw3KOIIoUiAz6ed5VqtnvPID2Maeub5D78C2d-82uRg4Iwg967ret0qiSQPTa7gGPdk=)\n[4] [unstructured.io](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQFFrqjHh47qPNGgQJUa9H5mFhiOcyqrVd8kU1VOe9Z61dPa4AVrwRany-AKEhOt5fEbj5lEo0kdWYPUP97Uv0jSv-45UhrUlWcfossxQ2TcP-jzQAtU8NHP64_CR6Exk5ZnM2XWTpIBq7jeBgs0oKjbwol4pLsCAB6Obj96eg==)\n[5] [unstructured.io](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQECnDUGA9k-hO2iWJgA6jdm5R3XKF1VoUp4SilKHVmQ0g5QSwvndMMP0vJG-oIpWHL9y8kVhnTeeVGhUoSYWFclXx5nAuCuwYh_lKiS1Nnxa_hpj0y3RWlfaRyyavApzzgV_3Nu4EqheheGlg4PoeO8TAoNlFX102dkfYHJ2eT-ZaEMqyhqgq0FjJqWJr83R-7kvQfo4XDVkFM=)\n[6] [unstructured.io](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQE4GJXc-1r2tdrS6kx7CvvGLSsmPrcYdOm5ymrKTylXbXuGRu_EOkR15EKDgvrl5-TEVnKKFh58AphJHR91VPbprYEYDt0MByLU-11j3t2lKxMqgD1aPX-1O2RGfbPdKO--xtiv--z-B76nSOgzjkHQBhRAdD-SSg6WgEJjwqmu64BXP0EsgxM=)\n[7] [unstructured.io](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQHOS7b6srHf1jHuUlx5UoEwP6LShtY5VvwfLMbj3FCisdnFWRfSFftBd4obSagWeEpwsb-wTpaqJTru8vTKcKPXYf0YRMAy7Ab2nH1fwDWBIV4PrcM0cFsgUKa5i1SC_fXFP6Ag1DhrC2IcKmwhzx9GiSq4pSgMuyZK92cqcuckofma1sjIG0ZKvQ==)\n[8] [context7.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQHa8bDDQh1H_oKeFpCSH7pdLUL6TNRTgVgvSQlsqI69JABqOjLTbMrVRoOseeiV5a3IVAW5CpG3GC0LgHVlIuCWLLYrZ5YgKe1QWWImgUmz1Q1xypjuz8THGpZkySmFpMlNCWk=)\n[9] [unstructured.io](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQFFrqjHh47qPNGgQJUa9H5mFhiOcyqrVd8kU1VOe9Z61dPa4AVrwRany-AKEhOt5fEbj5lEo0kdWYPUP97Uv0jSv-45UhrUlWcfossxQ2TcP-jzQAt